I go into the kitchen.
I need a coffee.
I meet Sven there.
He is a software tester at our company.
We are working together on the new project now.
"Hello, Maya!"
"Are you getting coffee too?" asks Sven.
"Yes, the project has just started," I answer.
"We have a lot to do."
We know each other by face, but we haven't talked much yet.
"How do you like Berlin so far?" he then asks me.
"Very much!"
"The spring here is really beautiful," I say.
"I have lived in Berlin for a year," Sven tells me.
We chat briefly about our work in the team.
I am a software engineer, and he tests my code at the end.
"Just let me know when your code is ready," says Sven.
"Then I will look for the bugs."
"I haven't made any bugs yet today," I joke.
Sven laughs loudly and takes his cup.
"We will see about that!" he answers.
We go back to work together.
